---
// /about: the founder story, in Brock's own words (do not reword it). Built, but NOT published until the owner says
// so (src/data/publish.ts). With about unpublished, getStaticPaths is empty, so the page isn't built, linked, or in
// the sitemap. Photos are in public/images (about-*.jpg), compressed, with the license plate blurred.
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import FinalCTA from "../../components/FinalCTA.astro";
import Breadcrumb from "../../components/Breadcrumb.astro";
import { published } from "../../data/publish";

export function getStaticPaths() {
	return published.about ? [{ params: { slug: undefined } }] : [];
}

const ORIGIN = "https://www.morium.one";
const aboutSchema = {
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "AboutPage",
	name: "About Morium",
	url: `${ORIGIN}/about`,
	about: { "@id": `${ORIGIN}/#organization` },
};
---

<Layout
	title="About Morium and Its Founder | Morium"
	description="Morium was built by Brock Livermore, a detailer who lost track of his own day and built the tool he wished he'd had."
	jsonLd={[aboutSchema]}
>
	<Header />
	<main class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-16 lg:px-8">
		<Breadcrumb items={[{ name: "Home", href: "/" }, { name: "About" }]} />
		<h1 class="mt-6 max-w-3xl font-display text-4xl leading-[1.1] font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">
			Built by a detailer who lost track of his own day.
		</h1>

		<div class="mt-12 grid items-start gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_340px]">
			<div class="max-w-2xl space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/75">
				<p>
					I started detailing in 2024, picking up a few jobs here and there. By the summer of 2025 it had
					turned into a real side business, and this past summer I did it full time.
				</p>
				<p>
					I began as an independent contractor, bringing my own supplies to other people's jobs. A few weeks
					in, I went out on my own as Livermore Auto Detailing and started running my own Google Local
					Services ads to find customers.
				</p>
				<p>
					That's when the work picked up, and the business side got messy. Some days I had three details
					booked and no clear picture of my day. Which address was first? Was this one an interior, a full
					detail, or a quick wash? What did the customer ask for when they booked? It all lived in texts,
					notes and my memory, and that's how things slip.
				</p>
			</div>
			<figure>
				<img
					src="/images/about-pressure-washing.jpg"
					alt="Pressure washing a car in a sunny driveway on an autumn afternoon, with the spray catching the light."
					width="1000"
					height="1500"
					class="aspect-[4/5] w-full rounded-2xl object-cover"
				/>
			</figure>
		</div>

		<div class="mt-12 max-w-2xl space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/75">
			<p class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-ink">So I built Morium.</p>
			<p>
				Morium is the tool I wish I'd had that summer. Every job sits in one place, with the address, the
				service, the price and the customer's notes. Customers can request a booking from your link at any
				hour. Reminders go out on their own, so people are home when you pull up. When the job is done, you
				send an invoice they can pay by card, and Morium can follow up for a review or a rebook.
			</p>
		</div>

		<figure class="mt-12">
			<img
				src="/images/about-steam-interior.jpg"
				alt="Steam rising off a car's interior door panel as it is steam cleaned, next to tan leather trim."
				width="1100"
				height="1100"
				loading="lazy"
				decoding="async"
				class="aspect-[16/9] w-full rounded-2xl object-cover object-[center_45%]"
			/>
		</figure>

		<div class="mt-12 grid items-start gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_340px]">
			<div class="max-w-2xl space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/75">
				<p>
					I kept it simple on purpose. A solo detailer gets everything on one easy plan, and a growing crew
					can add team members and roles when they need them. Morium is built for detailers first, with
					other service businesses coming next.
				</p>
				<p>
					Today I'm an entrepreneurship student at the University of Oklahoma, building Morium for
					detailers like me.
				</p>
				<p>
					When you open Morium, I want you to feel at ease. Your day is organized, your customers are
					reminded, and you can get back to the part of the job you actually enjoy.
				</p>
				<div class="pt-4">
					<p class="font-semibold text-ink">Brock Livermore</p>
					<p class="text-base text-ink/60">Founder, Morium</p>
				</div>
			</div>
			<figure>
				<img
					src="/images/about-driveway.jpg"
					alt="A person seen from behind pressure washing a light-colored car in a driveway, with a basketball hoop and autumn trees behind."
					width="1000"
					height="1500"
					loading="lazy"
					decoding="async"
					class="aspect-[4/5] w-full rounded-2xl object-cover"
				/>
			</figure>
		</div>
	</main>
	<FinalCTA />
	<Footer />
</Layout>
